      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Urban development in De Baarsjes began in the 1920s, when it was officially incorporated into Amsterdam.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Baarsjes",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "De Baarsjes is made up of four distinct neighbourhoods: Trompbuurt, Admiralenbuurt, Chassébuurt, and Postjesbuurt.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Baarsjes",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "vague"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "In 1990 De Baarsjes was designated a borough of Amsterdam as part of the city's administrative reorganization.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De_Baarsjes",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 2010 De Baarsjes merged with Bos en Lommer, Oud‑West, and Westerpark to form Amsterdam‑West.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
